  "definition": "Atmospheric correction estimates how a surface would appear without the scattering and absorption between it and a satellite sensor. The detector observes radiance, from which a calibrated top-of-atmosphere quantity may be produced. Bottom-of-atmosphere or surface reflectance is then retrieved through a physical model. It is not a direct measurement of the ground.",
